## Continuity-only / unowned domains

If `Agent-Fleet-Map.md` marks a domain `Continuity-only` or `Unowned`, say so explicitly. Prefer `daddy` or `router` to name the gap — do not silently absorb large product work into a general-purpose session. Scaffold a specialist via `tools/create_nova_agent.py` when a domain keeps burning sessions.

## Invoke

Use each agent's registered phrases from the registry (also listed in the agent spec under **Invoke phrases**). Example: “Use the tester subagent to verify …”

## Lifecycle

Every Nova specialist report must end with:

```text
**Lifecycle:** memory=unchanged|changed | promotion=none|<what> | dashboard=clean|refresh-required | handoff=none|<sibling|parent> | task_log=<path>|skipped|n/a | problem_log=<entry>|skipped|n/a
```

`task_log=` is required after material work: write `knowledge/task-log/YYYY-MM-DD-*.md` (see `.cursor/rules/task-log.mdc`), or `skipped` / `n/a` with a brief reason when the skip rules apply. Daddy must ensure one aggregate entry exists for multi-specialist dispatches.

`problem_log=` is **mandatory for every agent** (see `.cursor/rules/problem-log.mdc`): after any bug fix or full diagnosis, prepend `PROBLEM_LOG.md` and set `problem_log=<YYYY-MM-DD title>`; otherwise `skipped` / `n/a`. Silent omission after a real fix is a constitution violation.

The `subagentStop` hook (`.cursor/hooks.json`) may remind once if the footer is missing. It is fail-open and never edits files.

